From 78eca512781311077e47766438180d759475cf41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: you <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 23:53:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add BetterPosters-style dark/light auto sash-colour mode,
 sash/notch/bar font choice, Clean-mode dot separator

- New frost_reference=match ("Auto") mode for the frosted rating bar, notch
  badge and diagonal sash: keeps the poster colour's own lightness (can go
  genuinely dark on dark art) and auto-flips label text between black and
  white for contrast, instead of the old Pastel/Reference modes' hardcoded
  brightness floor that made a dark bar impossible.
- New label_font option (inter/bebas/oswald/playfair/notoserif/ubuntu) shared
  by the sash, notch badge and frosted bar, with a per-character fallback to
  Inter for the star glyph (none of the other bundled display faces carry a
  U+2605 glyph).
- New numeric_score_separator=dot option for Clean mode (rating_display_mode
  2): inserts a middle dot between the genre and the star rating.
- configurator.html: Reference Colour checkbox replaced with a 3-way
  Pastel/Reference/Auto segmented control (bar + sash panels, kept in sync),
  new Label Font dropdown, new Dot separator toggle for Clean mode.
All existing tests (383 passed, 1 skipped) still pass unchanged.
